-- migr:needs-session drop_check: SQLite's ALTER TABLE cannot drop a check constraint -- it renames a table, renames a column, adds a column and drops one, and does nothing else. This is performed by a table rebuild: copy the rows into a table carrying the new definition, drop the original, put the new one in its place, copy back, and restore every index and trigger. Building those statements means reading the table's current definition out of sqlite_schema, which is why it is compiled against the database rather than by Compile alone
